      "body": "  Imagine one pipeline stage owns two transformer blocks:\r\n```\r\n  Pipeline stage\r\n  ├── layers.0\r\n  │   ├── weight A\r\n  │   └── weight B\r\n  └── layers.1\r\n      ├── weight C\r\n      └── weight D\r\n```\r\n  GraphTrainer’s configured FSDP plan says:\r\n\r\n  bucket 0 = layers.0 parameters\r\n  bucket 1 = layers.1 parameters\r\n\r\n  The desired communication is therefore:\r\n\r\n  AG(A, B)   # layer 0 bucket\r\n  AG(C, D)   # layer 1 bucket\r\n\r\n  and similarly for reduce-scatter/all-reduce during backward.\r\n\r\n  ### What GraphPP did\r\n\r\n  GraphPP removes those collectives from the compute graph and creates separate actions:\r\n\r\n  UNSHARD action:\r\n      all parameter all-gathers\r\n\r\n  FORWARD:\r\n      compute only\r\n\r\n  BACKWARD:\r\n      compute only\r\n\r\n  REDUCE_GRAD action:\r\n      all gradient reductions\r\n\r\nChanging bucketing changes numerics, for bitwise numerics we have to keep the bucketing structure the same as eager.",
